Subject: [PATCH 22/44] tools: the mHC router's FP64 reference and the
 reduction orders it admits

Splitting the router's reduction looked like a free path to the 83 tok/s the
no-window build reaches, but CONTRIBUTING requires an FP64 reference before a
reduction order changes. This is that reference: over 528 real router inputs
from three prompts, physical layers 4, 5 and 27, both sites and both visits, it
compares the shipped 32-lane order against split-K at 8 and 4 slices, reporting
logit error and the error it induces in pre, post and mix.

All three agree to fp32 rounding: logit max |err| 2.40-2.47e-05, mean 1.48e-06,
with pre, post and mix within a few percent of each other. So the order is free
numerically -- and also buys nothing: the 8-slice kernel measures 34.1 tok/s
against 35.3, since at one row the loop over eight outputs costs more than the
parallelism adds. The shipped order stays, now with evidence rather than
assumption.
